WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.326 --> 00:00:03.328
Today is the feast of Saint Martin de Porres.

2
00:00:03.778 --> 00:00:07.181
He was born in Lima, Peru, in fifteen seventy-nine.

3
00:00:07.181 --> 00:00:09.450
His father was a Spanish nobleman.

4
00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:13.786
His mother, Ana, was a freed woman of African and Native descent.

5
00:00:13.786 --> 00:00:18.390
His father left, and his mother took in laundry to feed her children.

6
00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:23.978
Martin trained as a barber, which in those days also meant a kind of surgeon.

7
00:00:23.978 --> 00:00:26.713
As a young man he went to the Dominicans.

8
00:00:26.713 --> 00:00:30.850
At first he served as a helper, the lowest place in the house.

9
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:33.252
Later he took vows as a lay brother.

10
00:00:33.702 --> 00:00:34.770
He swept floors.

11
00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:39.507
He nursed the sick, any sick, rich or poor, Spanish, African or Native.

12
00:00:39.507 --> 00:00:42.042
He fed the hungry at the convent door.

13
00:00:42.042 --> 00:00:44.778
People called him the saint of the broom.

14
00:00:45.228 --> 00:00:50.832
There's a legend that he even talked the convent mice into moving out to the garden,

15
00:00:50.832 --> 00:00:54.302
and fed them there so they'd stop eating the linens.

16
00:00:54.302 --> 00:00:56.904
Legend or not, it tells you who he was.

17
00:00:57.354 --> 00:00:59.756
Saint Martin de Porres, pray for us.
